<title>UK: IBCA cuts SBC long term rating to AA plus. [CORRECTED 09:26 GMT]</title>
<headline>IBCA cuts SBC long term rating to AA plus. [CORRECTED 09:26 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>IBCA the European credit rating agency said on Friday it had cut the long-term rating of Swiss Bank Corporation to AA plus from AAA.</p>
<p>IBCA affirmed the short term A1 plus (correcting to add plus) rating.</p>
<p>&quot;The downgrade...reflects IBCA's concerns that there will be no rapid improvement in the quality of SBC's loan portfolio and that as a consequence of its increased exposure to investment banking the volatility of SBC's earnings has grown,&quot; IBCA said in a statement.</p>
</text>
